        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/id": "dd30c11b-b5c7-5075-8cd9-10d8eaf23ea0",
        ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/a4/a4e7fa23be759035d5765a80ed9d78b7fb7be560ec38fd24aedc172abd2b0b99.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/9b/9b7f2c9f69c8d8661ec513da0e8a3d0a8a7eb31d2826162aab0a2267ff659425.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $2$ squares left and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square right and $1$ square up. Thus $OX=2|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $9$ squares right and $6$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $3$ squares right and $2$ squares up. Thus $XC=3|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-2$ and $\\mu=3$."
      }
    }
