        ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/a5/a54112c9a79362b29b52e91f8b1773cd8adc7b7c6b7e2d8d83eeabb2f72a6f4b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/e1/e1de5bf39714b39ab3f2b0c154a48fa723de4fd96a86ffc06a9f7c799edf8986.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $2$ squares left and $4$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left and $2$ squares down. Thus $OX=2|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $2$ squares right and $2$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square down. Thus $XC=2|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-2\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=2\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=-2$."
