        ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/23/234549b34d36148a9fa6c907b68af712f3a5ff648508c9e839e3241d8e317cd0.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/ef/ef07cad1df5c81239c5fcddbf9579fb5ed6ae7a030a18b428b7291ad8b95783c.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $6$ squares right and $3$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $4$ squares left and $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=\\frac{3}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $2$ squares left and $2$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares left and $2$ squares up. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\mu=1$."
